		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Magic-wielding cobras towering ten feet high. Once a dominant species, they are now rare and reclusive, bitter to the last.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 16, <strong>HP</strong> 43, <strong>ATK</strong> 2 bite +7 (2d6 + poison) and 1 spell +7, <strong>MV</strong> near (climb), <strong>S</strong> +4, <strong>D</strong> +1, <strong>C</strong> +3, <strong>I</strong> +2, <strong>W</strong> +2, <strong>Ch</strong> +4, <strong>AL</strong> <strong>C</strong>, <strong>LV</strong> 9</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Agony (CHA Spell)</strong>. DC 14. One target in near takes 3d8 damage.</p><p></p><p><strong>Hypnotize (CHA Spell)</strong>. DC 13. Focus. One target in near range who can see naga is helplessly stupefied for duration.</p><p></p><p><strong>Poison</strong>. CON 15+ or paralyzed 1d4 rounds.</p><p></p><p><strong>Whispers (CHA Spell)</strong>. DC 12. Hostile spells cast on one target in near are DC 9 for 1d4 rounds.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
